        'If you notice bleeding or cramping, contact your doctor so they can check, usually with a scan and sometimes a blood test. In the meantime, use a sanitary pad rather than anything internal, and note what the bleeding is like so you can describe it. Many women who bleed in early pregnancy go on to have a healthy pregnancy, so as far as you can, try to have it checked calmly rather than assume the worst.',
