  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-CANI-DO-010',
    number: 77,
    month: 2,
    question: 'Is it safe to travel during pregnancy?',
    category: 'Work & Travel (Can I > Do)',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'In a healthy pregnancy, travel is generally safe, and the second trimester is usually the most comfortable time. Early pregnancy travel is fine too, though nausea and tiredness can make it less pleasant, so shorter trips are easier for now. Do check with your doctor before long, international or high-altitude travel, or if your pregnancy is high-risk.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Most travel carries no special risk in an uncomplicated pregnancy. The main practical concerns are comfort and, on long journeys, sitting still for hours, which raises the risk of a blood clot in the legs (called deep vein thrombosis) for everyone, a little more so in pregnancy. Flying is considered safe before around 36 weeks, after which airlines often restrict it.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'On any journey over a few hours, by car, train or plane, move and stretch your legs regularly, walk when you can, stay hydrated, and wear loose, comfortable clothing. Always wear your seatbelt, with the lap belt below your bump and across your hips. Carry your pregnancy records, keep snacks handy for nausea, and know where you could get care at your destination. For long, international or high-altitude travel, or if your pregnancy is high-risk, check with your doctor first, and avoid areas with mosquito-borne illnesses like Zika or malaria.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Check with your doctor before long, international or high-altitude travel, or if your pregnancy is high-risk.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Pregnancy does not mean staying home; a little planning lets you travel comfortably and safely.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Travel is generally safe; the second trimester is most comfortable.',
        'Move your legs and hydrate on trips over a few hours.',
        'Wear the seatbelt low, under your bump.',
        'Flying is usually fine before about 36 weeks.',
        'Check with your doctor for long, international or high-risk travel.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-CANI-DO-009',
      'PREG-CANI-DO-013',
      'PREG-CANI-DO-008',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-013',
    number: 78,
    month: 2,
    question: 'What warning signs mean I should call my doctor?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    held: true,
    heldNote: 'Yes (safety reference)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Most pregnancy symptoms are uncomfortable but harmless. A few, though, are worth acting on: call your doctor promptly for heavy bleeding, severe tummy pain, a severe headache with blurred vision or sudden swelling of the face or hands, a fever, persistent vomiting, fainting, or one-sided leg pain or breathlessness. This is about awareness, not fear; most pregnancies never involve any of them.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Certain symptoms can occasionally signal a problem that is best checked early, when it is most treatable. Knowing your own "normal" makes it easier to notice when something is genuinely different.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Contact your doctor promptly if you have heavy vaginal bleeding, or bleeding with pain; severe or persistent tummy pain; a severe headache that will not ease, especially with blurred vision, seeing spots, or sudden swelling of the face or hands; a fever; persistent vomiting where you cannot keep fluids down; fainting or severe dizziness; pain, swelling or redness in one leg, or trouble breathing; or painful urination. Later in pregnancy, a noticeable drop in your baby\'s movements or a gush of fluid also warrant a call. Above all, if something simply feels wrong, it is always okay to check.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Any of the signs above deserves a prompt call; if you cannot reach your doctor and feel unwell, go to your nearest hospital.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Keeping a short mental list of these signs is not about worrying, it is quiet confidence, so you know exactly when to reach out.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Most symptoms are normal; only a few need prompt action.',
        'Call for heavy bleeding, severe pain, or a severe headache with vision changes or swelling.',
        'Call for fever, persistent vomiting, fainting, leg pain or breathlessness.',
        'Later, reduced baby movements or leaking fluid warrant a call.',
        'Trust your instinct; if something feels wrong, check.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-001',
      'PREG-HEALTH-011',
      'PREG-HEALTH-002',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-014',
    number: 79,
    month: 2,
    question: 'What is a molar pregnancy?',
    category: 'Loss & Difficult Journeys',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (loss; gentle register, no monetization)',
    held: true,
    heldNote: 'Yes (escalation guardrail)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A molar pregnancy is a rare condition where the tissue that would normally become the placenta grows abnormally, so the pregnancy cannot develop as usual. It is uncommon, and although it means this pregnancy will not continue, it is very treatable.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'It happens by chance at fertilisation, not because of anything you did. In a molar pregnancy, abnormal placental tissue grows and produces unusually high levels of the pregnancy hormone hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin). This can cause signs like vaginal bleeding, often dark or brownish, more severe than usual nausea, or a womb that grows faster than expected, and it is usually picked up on an early scan.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If a scan shows a molar pregnancy, your doctor will explain the next steps, which involve gently removing the tissue and then checking your hCG levels over the following weeks until they return to normal. This follow-up matters, because occasionally the tissue can persist and need a little more treatment. The reassuring part is that after treatment, most women go on to have a healthy pregnancy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'This is diagnosed and managed by your doctor; contact them about heavy or dark bleeding or severe vomiting so it can be checked.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'A molar pregnancy is frightening to hear about, but it is rare, treatable, and not your fault, and support is there if you need it.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'A molar pregnancy is a rare, abnormal growth of placental tissue.',
        'It happens by chance, not because of anything you did.',
        'Signs include unusual bleeding, severe nausea, high hCG, fast womb growth.',
        'It is found on a scan and treated by removing the tissue.',
        'Follow-up hCG checks are needed; most women later have a healthy pregnancy.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-012',
      'PREG-HEALTH-015',
      'PREG-EMOTION-004',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-015',
    number: 80,
    month: 2,
    question: 'What is a vanishing twin?',
    category: 'Loss & Difficult Journeys',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (loss; gentle register, no monetization)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A vanishing twin is when an early scan shows twins, but one twin stops developing and is gently reabsorbed by the body, usually in the first trimester. In most cases the remaining twin continues to grow and develop normally.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'It happens early, often before a heartbeat is well established, and is thought to be due to a chance difference in how that twin was developing, not anything the parents did or could prevent. Because it occurs so early, the tissue is usually reabsorbed naturally, and there is often no symptom at all, though some women have light spotting or mild cramping.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If this happens, your doctor will monitor the pregnancy with scans to check on the surviving twin, who usually does well. Emotionally, it can bring mixed and confusing feelings, relief for the continuing pregnancy alongside a real sense of loss, and both are valid.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Your doctor will monitor the surviving twin; contact them about any bleeding or cramping so it can be checked.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Feeling both grief and hope at once is understandable, and support is there for you if the loss feels heavy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'A vanishing twin is when one early twin stops developing and is reabsorbed.',
        'It usually happens in the first trimester.',
        'The remaining twin usually continues normally.',
        'There may be light spotting or no symptoms.',
        'Mixed emotions are natural; support is available.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-005',
      'PREG-HEALTH-012',
      'PREG-EMOTION-004',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-CANI-EAT-006',
    number: 81,
    month: 2,
    question: 'Is it safe to eat street food and outside food in pregnancy?',
    category: 'Food (Can I > Eat)',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Eat',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Street food like pani puri, chaat and cut fruit is best kept to a minimum in pregnancy, because the main risk is a stomach infection from unhygienic handling or water, not the food itself. If you do have it, choose freshly cooked, piping-hot items, skip anything raw or watery, and contact your doctor if you get a bad stomach with fever or severe cramps.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Your immunity is naturally a little lower in pregnancy, so contaminated food or water can more easily cause food poisoning, which can leave you dehydrated and unwell. The usual culprits are the water in golgappa or chutneys, cut fruit and raw toppings left in the open, reused frying oil, and undercooked egg or meat. Monsoon raises the risk further.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If a craving strikes, make it safer: pick a busy, clean-looking stall that cooks fresh, eat it hot rather than lukewarm, avoid raw chutneys, cut fruit and ice, and carry your own water. Better still, recreate favourites at home with filtered water and clean ingredients, where you control the hygiene.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'See your doctor for vomiting or diarrhoea you cannot keep on top of, or that comes with fever, blood or severe cramps.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'You do not have to give up every chaat craving, just make it hot, fresh and hygienic, or bring it into your own kitchen.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'The risk is infection from hygiene and water, not the dish itself.',
        'Lowered immunity makes food poisoning more likely.',
        'If you indulge, eat it freshly cooked and piping hot.',
        'Skip raw chutneys, cut fruit, ice and unfiltered water.',
        'Home versions with filtered water are safest.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-CANI-EAT-001',
      'PREG-CANI-DRINK-003',
      'PREG-CANI-EAT-002',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-CANI-EAT-007',
