  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-CANI-DRINK-004',
    number: 83,
    month: 2,
    question: 'Is coconut water good during pregnancy?',
    category: 'Nutrition (Can I > Drink)',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Drink',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Coconut water (nariyal pani) is a safe, hydrating and refreshing choice in pregnancy, enjoyed in normal amounts. It will not, however, make your baby fairer or give thicker hair, those are myths.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Fresh coconut water is naturally low in calories and rich in electrolytes like potassium and magnesium, so it hydrates well, especially in Indian summers, and some women find it soothes nausea and acidity. What it cannot do is change your baby\'s complexion or hair, which are set by genetics, not by anything you drink. It also does not replace a balanced diet or your prescribed supplements.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Have a glass or two a day if you enjoy it, ideally fresh and unsweetened. There is no need to drink litres of it for a "fair baby"; that expectation simply cannot be met. If you have gestational diabetes or your doctor watches your potassium, check your intake with them.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Check your intake with your doctor if you have gestational diabetes or have been told to watch potassium.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
