  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-GEN-005',
    number: 94,
    month: 2,
    question: 'Do I really need to "eat for two"?',
    category: 'Nutrition / General',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'You do not need to "eat for two" in pregnancy. Your baby needs better nutrition, not double the food, and your extra calorie needs are quite small, especially early on.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In the first trimester you need almost no extra calories, rising to only about 300 to 350 more a day in the second trimester and a little more in the third, roughly a bowl of dal-rice or a banana with some nuts, not a second plate. Overeating mainly adds excess weight, which raises the chance of gestational diabetes, high blood pressure and delivery complications. What your baby draws on is the quality of your food, its vitamins, minerals and protein.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Focus on nutrient-dense meals, dals, vegetables, whole grains, dairy, fruit and protein, rather than larger portions or extra sweets and fried foods. Eat to comfortable fullness and let your steady weight gain, tracked by your doctor, guide you rather than the old "eat for two" idea.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Your doctor tracks your weight; ask them if you are unsure how much more to eat.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Pregnancy asks for a richer plate, not a bigger one; quality is what truly nourishes your baby.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'You don\'t need to eat for two.',
        'Extra needs are about 300 to 350 calories a day from the second trimester.',
        'Overeating raises weight, diabetes and blood-pressure risks.',
        'Quality of food matters more than quantity.',
        'Let steady, tracked weight gain guide you.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-BODY-020',
