        'In pregnancy, mosquito-borne infections can hit harder and, in some cases, affect the baby, so health bodies advise pregnant women to prevent bites rather than risk infection. India sees seasonal dengue, malaria and chikungunya, especially in and after the monsoon, which makes protection genuinely useful.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Use a mosquito repellent that is safe in pregnancy, repellents containing DEET (a common repellent ingredient) are considered safe when used as directed, and apply as per the label. Sleep under a mosquito net, use screens on windows, and wear full-sleeved clothing at dawn and dusk when mosquitoes are active. Remove standing water around the home where mosquitoes breed. If you use coils or vaporisers, keep the room well ventilated, and prefer nets and repellents where you can.',
