    question: 'When does the baby\'s heartbeat start, and can I hear it?',
    category: 'Baby Development',
    applicability: 'Month 2 (weeks 5 to 8)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Your baby\'s heartbeat usually begins around 5 to 6 weeks, and can often be seen flickering on an early ultrasound from about 6 to 7 weeks. If a very early scan does not show it yet, that is usually just a matter of timing rather than a problem, and a repeat scan a week or so later brings clarity.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In these first weeks a tiny heart is forming and starting to beat, even before it is fully built, which is why a scan around 6 to 7 weeks can show that flicker and a rate that is often faster than your own. Seeing a heartbeat is genuinely reassuring, because once it is confirmed at this stage the chance of miscarriage drops considerably. Before about 6 weeks the embryo is simply too small for the heartbeat to be picked up, so an early "not yet" is common and not a bad sign on its own.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'There is nothing you need to do to "start" the heartbeat; it happens on its own. If your doctor arranges an early scan and the timing is borderline, try not to read too much into a single picture, since dates are not always exact and a follow-up scan is standard. The handheld device (Doppler) that lets you listen to the heartbeat is usually used at antenatal visits a bit later, from around 12 weeks, and the detailed look at the heart happens at the anomaly scan around 18 to 22 weeks.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Your doctor will arrange and interpret early scans; ask them if any timing or finding is unclear.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'One of pregnancy\'s quiet wonders is that the heart begins to beat before it is even finished forming, working long before your baby draws a first breath.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'The heartbeat usually begins around 5 to 6 weeks.',
