    sensitivity: 'Yes (loss, gentle register)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'No ordinary food causes a miscarriage. The great majority of early miscarriages happen for chromosomal reasons in the pregnancy, not because of anything you ate. A few foods are worth avoiding for infection or safety reasons, but that is different from "causing" a miscarriage.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'More than eight in ten miscarriages occur in the first trimester, and most are due to the pregnancy not developing as it should from the very start, something no diet causes or prevents. The popular Indian fears around papaya and pineapple are largely myths: only unripe or semi-ripe papaya (which has latex) and very large amounts of pineapple are traditionally avoided as a precaution, while ripe fruit in normal amounts is fine and even nourishing. The foods genuinely worth avoiding, like alcohol, raw or undercooked meat and eggs, unpasteurised cheese and high-mercury fish, are risky because of infection or harmful substances, not because they trigger miscarriage.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Eat a normal, balanced diet, skip the genuinely risky foods, and enjoy ripe fruit without fear. Most importantly, if you have had a loss, please know it was almost certainly not caused by something you ate.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'See your doctor for any bleeding, cramping or pain, and for advice on your own diet if your pregnancy is high-risk.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'So much pregnancy food advice is passed down with love but not evidence; the freeing truth is that a miscarriage is rarely, if ever, your plate\'s fault.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'No ordinary food reliably causes miscarriage.',
        'Most early miscarriages are chromosomal, not diet-related.',
        'Papaya and pineapple fears are largely myths; avoid only unripe papaya and large amounts of pineapple.',
        'Do avoid alcohol, raw or undercooked foods, unpasteurised cheese, high-mercury fish.',
        'A past loss is almost never something you ate.',
      ]),
