  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BODY-030',
    number: 103,
    month: 2,
    question: 'What symptoms show up when? An early-pregnancy symptom map',
    category: 'Body & Symptoms',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Early pregnancy symptoms tend to arrive in a rough order rather than all at once, and they differ a lot from woman to woman. Knowing the usual pattern can make the early weeks feel less confusing.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'As pregnancy hormones rise, the body responds in stages. Often the earliest signs are a missed period, tender breasts and tiredness, followed within a few weeks by nausea, a heightened sense of smell, and needing to pee more often. Nausea commonly peaks around weeks 8 to 10 and eases for many by the second trimester. Later come the more visible changes: a growing bump, skin changes and, later still, baby\'s movements. Having few symptoms, or many, are both normal; symptoms are not a reliable measure of how the pregnancy is going.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Use the pattern as a loose guide, not a checklist. If a symptom you had suddenly settles, that is usually fine, and if new ones appear, they often fit the timeline. What is worth prompt attention, at any stage, is heavy bleeding, severe pain, a high fever, or the specific warning signs your doctor has flagged.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'See your doctor for the warning signs, or if any symptom feels severe or worrying rather than merely uncomfortable.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Early pregnancy can feel like a string of surprises; seeing them as a familiar sequence rather than random events tends to make the whole experience calmer.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Symptoms usually arrive in a rough order, not all at once.',
        'Early: missed period, tender breasts, fatigue; then nausea, smell sensitivity, frequent urination.',
        'Nausea often peaks weeks 8 to 10, easing by the second trimester.',
        'Few or many symptoms are both normal.',
        'Severe bleeding, pain or fever always deserve a check.',
      ]),
    ],
