    number: 104,
    month: 2,
    question: 'When will I start showing, and why do bumps differ?',
    category: 'Body & Symptoms',
    applicability: 'First to second trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Most women do not have a visible bump in the second month; you usually start to show around 12 to 16 weeks, often later in a first pregnancy. How soon and how much you show varies with your build and height, whether this is a first or a later pregnancy, your abdominal muscles, your womb\'s position, and whether you are carrying more than one baby. Any "bump" this early is more likely to be bloating.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'In these early weeks your womb is still low in the pelvis, so there is little to see from outside even though a lot is happening within. The factors above are why two women at exactly the same stage can look quite different: a later pregnancy or a shorter frame tends to show sooner, while strong abdominal muscles or a womb that tilts back can show later.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Try not to compare your belly to anyone else\'s or to a timeline online. A smaller or later bump does not mean a smaller or less healthy baby. Comfortable, roomy clothing helps as bloating comes and goes.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Mention it at your visits if you have concerns; your doctor tracks your bump\'s growth later in pregnancy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Every bump keeps its own schedule; when you show says nothing about how well your baby is growing.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'You usually show around 12 to 16 weeks, often later in a first pregnancy.',
        'An early "bump" now is more likely bloating.',
        'Build, height, muscles, womb position and twins all affect timing.',
        'A smaller or later bump does not mean a smaller baby.',
        'Don\'t compare your belly to others.',
      ]),
