    number: 107,
    month: 2,
    question: 'Is my IVF pregnancy more fragile in these early weeks?',
    category: 'High-Risk & Special Pregnancies',
    applicability: 'First trimester',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (fertility, gentle register)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'In the early weeks an in vitro fertilisation (IVF) pregnancy carries a slightly higher miscarriage risk than average, mostly because of the reasons behind needing fertility treatment, not the treatment itself. The reassuring part: once a heartbeat is seen around 6 to 7 weeks, the risk drops considerably, and after 12 weeks it is similar to any pregnancy.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'The slightly higher early risk is linked to factors like age or underlying fertility issues, and to a marginally higher chance of chromosomal differences, rather than to IVF harming the pregnancy. This is why fertility teams monitor these weeks closely, with early blood tests such as beta hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin), an early viability scan, and often continued hormone (progesterone) support. Each reassuring milestone, a rising hCG, a heartbeat, a good dating scan, meaningfully lowers the odds of loss.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Keep to the monitoring and any medicines your fertility team has prescribed, and do not stop hormone support on your own. Rest, eat well, and lean on your clinic for questions; the early weeks are understandably anxious, and support helps.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Stay in close touch with your fertility team, and follow their schedule for scans, blood tests and medicines.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'These early IVF weeks can feel especially tender after all it took to get here; each small milestone is a genuine, steadying step forward.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'IVF pregnancies have a slightly higher early miscarriage risk, mostly from underlying factors, not IVF itself.',
        'Risk drops considerably once a heartbeat is seen (about 6 to 7 weeks).',
        'After 12 weeks it is similar to any pregnancy.',
        'Expect close monitoring: hCG tests, early scan, hormone support.',
        'Don\'t stop prescribed support on your own.',
      ]),
    ],
